### Page 2 of 3

```text
Planning Commission
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
September 26, 2024
PZ-24-00073 PC 9.26.24 Meeting Packet
Attachments:
Cate Cundall, Associate Planner, reported that a Zone Change from A-1 to AR had
been requested by Sundance Kid Properties, LLC, for Tract 2, The Horse Creek
Ranch, 2nd Filing. The application has been submitted to change to a zone district
that would allow for smaller lots.
An application for an Administrative Plat was also submitted to divide the 12.00 acre
parcel into two 6 acre parcels for residential use. This application will be approved by
the BOCC and is included only for informational purposes.
Prior planning actions initiated in 2014, for the Horse Creek Ranch Subdivision
include a Variance to divide Tract 19 and a plat revision for a boundary line
adjustment between Tracts 18 and 19. The Variance request did not receive approval
by the Planning Commission and was later withdrawn by the applicant. The Horse
Creek Ranch, 2nd Filing was approved by the BOCC on November 4, 2014.
Staff recommends one condition to be added to the approval of the zone change:
1. The Administrative Plat for the Horse Creek Ranch Subdivision, 4th Filing, must be
approved by the Laramie County Board of Commissioners.
Shane Hansen, agent for applicant, was present to answer questions.
Acting Chairman Stadel open the Public Hearing for comments. Comments were
heard from:
1. Robert Hoard - 11311 Doc Holliday Loop - Changing the zone district to allow for
splits will devalue surrounding properties. He purchased his home thinking that no
adjacent homes would be built.
2. Brad Hoard - 7910 Kepler Drive - Prior owner of 11311 Doc Holliday Loop who is
not in favor of the proposed zone change since it would increase the density of
housing in the subdivision.
3. Tim Watsek - 3960 Butch Cassidy Trail - The intent of the subdivision were 10 acre
lots and the assurance that minimum lot sizes would not be changed.
4. Jim Schepp - 11447 Doc Holliday Loop - Not in favor of the zone change. If smaller
lots are wanted they can be found in other subdivisions.
Planning Commission members asked if there were covenants for the subdivision
and the reasoning behind the disapproval of the earlier planning action.
Hearing no further comments the public hearing was closed and Acting Chairman
Stadel called for a motion and discussion.
Mark Smith moved, seconded by Natacha Gaspar to adopt the findings of
